# X identity and xIdentities

Apply when editing identity resolution, IndexedDB identity rows, or background handlers that read/write `xIdentities`.

## NIP-39 and proof discovery

- Merge and verify NIP-39 kind `10011` X links with matching `twitter` and `twitter_id` proof tags.
- Treat `10011` as the user's current claim (latest replaceable event) that narrows which X account is linked; accept it only after the referenced X proof post verifies.
- Persist durable Nostr↔X bindings in IndexedDB `xIdentities`; do not auto-create kind `10011` when a proof is discovered — the user publishes `10011` explicitly.
- Page-world may initiate authenticated GraphQL proof search (e.g. `SearchTimeline`) only when `xIdentities` lacks a verified binding: (1) extension X-pane open / explicit self CHECK with `scanPage`, or (2) the user clicks Trust on another X account.
- Passive allowlisted GraphQL may also emit loose NIP-39-ish proof candidates (`REPORT_X_PROOF_CANDIDATES`); the service worker must oEmbed-revalidate before any `xProof*` write. Prefer newer proof posts via GraphQL `created_at` (`xProofPostedAt`) — older proof posts must not overwrite newer ones.
- Forward only validated proof match results (`postId`, handle, proof text) across the content boundary.

## xIdentities column rules

- Only a found X proof post may write `xProof*` fields; only kind `10011` may write `nip39*` fields.
- Page observations may write `displayName` and `iconPath` (pbs.twimg.com path stem only).
- A `nip39` event must never invent or override proof fields.
- Either side (`xProof*` or `nip39*`) may arrive first. After every `xIdentities` field write, re-run status sync. When both sides are column-aligned and the row is not yet `verified`, attempt live `verifyNip39Proof` (existing oEmbed + profile→ID). Success → `verified` and graph rebuild. Column alignment alone is not enough; search-only writes do not add a new fetch. Already-verified aligned rows stay verified without re-fetching.
- Broadcast `X_IDENTITY_UPDATED` when derived status changes (`statusChanged: true`) so the extension UI and x.com content script refresh trust immediately. Chrome-only row updates (displayName/iconPath) may broadcast with `statusChanged: false` for Users/Graph lists — content must not `invalidateAll` on those.

## Storage notes

- Single durable table `xIdentities`, keyed by `twitterId`. No `handleAliases`, `identityObservations`, or `identityResolutionCache`.
- Singular latest columns: `handle`, `displayName`, `iconPath`. Handle is mutable (X.com URLs / proof search); it is not a lookup key.
- `updatedAt` = row data changed; `lastSeen` = touch on ingest (always bumped).
- Backend lookups always by `twitterId`. NIP-39 wire still requires both `twitter` and `twitter_id` tags.

## Storage split

- Raw signed events, reducer indexes, relay cursors, identity records, and the durable outbox live in IndexedDB.
- Reserve `chrome.storage.local` for small settings and the encrypted key vault only.
